msgid "Migration Guide"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Today, we announce the availability of Quarkus 2.5.0.Final which comes with "
"the following main improvements:"
msgstr ""

msgid "Upgrade to GraalVM/Mandrel 21.3"
msgstr ""

msgid "Support for JPA entity listeners for Hibernate ORM in native mode"
msgstr ""

msgid "Ability to add HTTP headers to responses"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Various usability improvements in extensions and our dev mode/testing "
"infrastructure"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"To migrate from 2.4, please refer to https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/"
"wiki/Migration-Guide-2.5[our migration guide]."
msgstr ""

msgid "What&#8217;s new?"
msgstr ""

msgid "GraalVM/Mandrel 21.3"
msgstr ""

msgid "GraalVM/Mandrel 21.3 is the recommended version for Quarkus 2.5."
msgstr ""

msgid "Hibernate ORM"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.5 adds support for JPA entity listeners, including in native mode."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Until now, they were not really supported and were working in JVM mode only."
msgstr ""

msgid "Adding headers with quarkus.http.header"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"With `quarkus.http.header`, you can easily add headers to your HTTP "
"responses:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"See the http://quarkus.io/guides/http-reference#additional-http-headers[HTTP "
"reference documentation] for more information."
msgstr ""

msgid "Security"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Some well known providers such as `GitHub` or `LinkedIn` are not `OpenId "
"Connect` but `OAuth2` providers which support the `authorization code flow`, "
"for example, link:https://docs.github.com/en/developers/apps/building-oauth-"
"apps/authorizing-oauth-apps[GitHub OAuth2] and link:https://docs.microsoft."
"com/en-us/linkedin/shared/authentication/authorization-code-flow[LinkedIn "
"OAuth2]."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.5 supports these providers as explained in the link:/guides/"
"security-openid-connect-web-authentication#integration-with-github-and-other-"
"oauth2-providers[Using OpenID Connect (OIDC) to Protect Web Applications "
"using Authorization Code Flow] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Using RESTEasy Reactive, it is now possible to filter the JSON output based "
"on the role of the user using the `@SecureField` annotation:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the example above, the `lastName` field will be included in the JSON "
"output only if the user has the `admin` role."
msgstr ""

msgid "Flyway"
msgstr ""

msgid "Flyway was updated to 8.0."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is now possible to generate initial migration scripts from the Hibernate "
"ORM generated schema from the Dev UI."
msgstr ""

msgid "Reactive Microsoft SQL Server client"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Reactive Microsoft SQL Server client now supports encryption."
msgstr ""

msgid "Infinispan"
msgstr ""

msgid "The Infinispan client extension has been upgraded to 13.0.0.Final."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The development/test infrastructure for Infinispan got major improvements in "
"the form of a test resource and a dev service:\n"
"you can automatically start Infinispan in dev mode and in your tests."
msgstr ""

msgid "Oracle"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"A Dev Service for Oracle has been added:\n"
"start your Oracle database automatically in dev and test mode."
msgstr ""

msgid "Camel 3.13.0"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Camel Quarkus extensions have been upgraded to Camel 3.13.0 version, that "
"brings a list of improvements and fixes. Check the https://camel.apache.org/"
"releases/release-3.13.0/[Camel 3.13.0 release notes]."
msgstr ""

msgid "Kubernetes extensions"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"It is now possible to define service bindings using Quarkus configuration as "
"explained in the link:/guides/deploying-to-"
"kubernetes#service_binding[Deploying to Kubernetes] guide."
msgstr ""

msgid "Quarkus Maven plugin - Go offline"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The default Maven feature to go offline doesn't download the full set of "
"Quarkus artifacts\n"
"as some artifacts (the deployment/build ones) are resolved by the Quarkus "
"Maven plugin and are not part of the regular dependencies."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Quarkus 2.5 introduces the `quarkus:go-offline` goal to cover this "
"requirement."
msgstr ""

msgid "Note that the same feature will come to the Gradle plugin very soon."
msgstr ""

msgid "Testing"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"When testing command line applications using `@QuarkusMain`, you can define "
"the command line parameters in a `QuarkusTestProfile` by implementing "
"`commandLineParameters()`."
msgstr ""

